# Every text file is LF in every checkout, Windows included.
#
# Git for Windows checks text out as CRLF by default. That breaks three
# things here: mutate.py finds its mutations by exact text, and "\n" does not
# match "\r\n"; ltcplay/version.py hashes the bytes of the program, so the
# same commit would report a different build id on Windows; and the Mac
# launchers are bash, which reads a CRLF line as a command ending in "\r".
* text=auto eol=lf

